; A plain `dune build' builds what ships, and nothing under tests.
;
; Without this stanza dune assumes (deps (alias_rec all)) here, which reaches
; every directory in the tree: building would compile all hundred-odd test
; executables and run the eighty-two that record their output. A subdirectory
; cannot opt out of that, since the recursion asks each directory for its all
; alias and never for its default.
;
; `dune build @runtest' and `dune build @check' name what they need and are
; unaffected.

(alias
 (name default)
 (deps
  (alias_rec lib/all)
  (alias_rec bin/all)
  (alias_rec linux/all)))
